WEBVTT

00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:05.220
You mentioned having an entertainment 
duel, didn't you?

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:09.760
But your way of dueling is mere self-satisfaction.

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.930
It is a far cry from entertainment!

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.130
You lack the power to climb to 
the summit where I stand!

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.570
Then, I attack directly with 
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:29.540
Red Hot Crimson Hell Burning!

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.780
Kneel before your king!

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:40.950
Yuya!

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.550
D-Wheels.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.800
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:52.490
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:55.950
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.100
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:35.500
Shattered Entertainment

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:40.160
That was the special match from the 
Friendship Cup opening ceremony.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:43.310
Naturally, the winner was our King of Duelists,

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:45.900
Jack Atlas!

00:02:47.450 --> 00:03:08.200
Jack! Jack! Jack! Jack!

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:12.600
Man, Jack really is great!

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:13.950
Did you see that, Yuzu?

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.740
Yuya!

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:18.810
Yuya!

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:21.140
Roger. We'll bring her in.

00:03:23.410 --> 00:03:24.720
Excuse me...

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.780
Please move out of the way. Hey...

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:28.740
Yuya!

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:34.790
My...

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.080
My father taught me this way of dueling...

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.420
I won't let you mock it, Jack!

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.630
Yuya! Yuya!

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:51.380
Hey, Yuzu... It's okay, calm down.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.800
No need to worry so.

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:00.410
What are you doing? Let me go!

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.250
Are you guys with security? What do you want?

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.320
Why are you trying to arrest participants 
in the Friendship Cup?

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.860
Give me a break!

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:13.470
Now, come with us peacefully.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:21.980
The Administrative Council has ordered 
us to bring them to the dormitory.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:25.210
The Public Order Bureau has 
no authority to interfere.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.820
You're not with security?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.290
Those old fools! They did it again...

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:38.040
Forgive us for the trouble.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.330
We will lead you from here.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.790
Wait a minute!

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.060
Yuya... Where's Yuya?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.510
Don't worry.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.720
He's a Friendship Cup participant, as well.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.040
He's been brought to the same dormitory.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:06.730
Ow...

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:11.720
Let's see...

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:16.870
I remember taking part in the Friendship 
Cup opening ceremonies.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.030
That's right! I lost to Jack Atlas.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:43.030
Where... am I?

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:46.160
Awake, are you?

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.240
Do forgive me...

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.400
I didn't mean to startle you.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.960
When did you come in?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.370
And why are you transparent?!

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:02.990
This is 3D Vision. We aren't actually here.

00:06:02.990 --> 00:06:06.190
But you can see and talk to us.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:09.210
All participants in the Friendship Cup...

00:06:09.210 --> 00:06:12.140
...are our guests.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:16.360
And are under our surveillance. Right, chairman?

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:17.130
Yes.

00:06:17.620 --> 00:06:24.660
You're in a penthouse at the top of the 
Administrative Council Building.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:28.620
It has first-rate hotel facilities.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.840
Is it comfortable?

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:35.310
I need to know where the others are. 
Gongenzaka and Serena...

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:37.230
No need to worry.

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.680
They are all here.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.540
In the same building.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.710
Although in different rooms.

00:06:42.970 --> 00:06:44.420
They're all here?

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:51.520
The sixteen of you will spend the 
tournament in these penthouses.

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:55.480
However, you can only remain for 
as long as you keep winning.

00:06:55.480 --> 00:06:57.750
If you lose, you'll be kicked out immediately.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:06:59.630
In that case...

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:02.400
Since I lost to Jack, I can't participate 
in the tournament?

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.520
That was an exhibition. Not part 
of the actual tournament.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.280
Right, chairman?

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.650
Yes, those who are asked to leave

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:14.520
are the ones who lose in the Friendship Cup proper.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.450
That was an unaffiliated match, so don't worry.

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:20.780
But the next time you lose...

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.370
Anyway, if you want to stay here...

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:25.400
...you just need to keep winning.

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.130
That is all we wanted to tell you.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.620
Well, goodbye.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.260
Hey, wait! Is Yuzu...

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:39.270
If Yuzu's really taking part in 
the Friendship Cup, too,

00:07:39.670 --> 00:07:41.730
she'll also be in this building!

00:07:47.590 --> 00:07:48.550
It isn't opening?

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.600
Hey! Someone!

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.520
No one's there?

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.620
If you are, answer me!

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.170
There really isn't anyone there?

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.980
I'm sorry, but we'll be moving you there.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:09.330
Public Order Bureau Director Roget 
seems to have it out for you.

00:08:09.610 --> 00:08:14.290
In a normal hotel, security might 
come after you at any time.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:18.580
This is all to ensure your safety. Right, chairman?

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:22.780
Yes. I fear it may be rather stifling.

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:27.320
But within that building, you can 
conduct yourselves freely.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.880
Thank you for your consideration.

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.580
I have no objections to Layra 
entering the tournament,

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:38.380
or to staying in the same facility 
as the other duelists.

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:55.290
Man, this is heaven!

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:59.050
Participating in the Friendship Cup 
sure gets you good treatment.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:02.340
I wish I could stay here forever...

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:09.060
My Odd-Eyes and Ute's Dark Rebellion...

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:14.780
Back then, the two dragons 
seemed to call to each other.

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:22.330
And afterward, Hugo appeared and 
summoned a dragon, as well.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:29.620
Could it be reacting to Hugo's dragon again?

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:32.650
If Hugo's here, Yuzu might be nearby!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.800
Yuzu! Are you here?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.670
If you can hear me, say something!

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.950
I've come across dimensions to save you!

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.680
Gongenzaka and Sawatari are with me, also!

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:45.360
Kurosaki and Dennis are, too! And Serena!

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.860
They've come because they wanted to save you!

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:52.140
The principal, Futoshi, Ayu, Tatsuya, my mom...

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:54.040
They're all worried about you!

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:57.530
So I swear I'll save you!

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:01.130
And I'll use my entertainment duel to 
stop the war, and return the smiles

00:10:01.130 --> 00:10:03.480
to everyone, in every dimension!

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.420
But your way of dueling is mere self-satisfaction.

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:11.560
It is a far cry from entertainment!

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:17.590
Can I do it?

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:19.510
Can I really stop the fighting?

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:22.840
Can I really bring smiles to everyone's faces?

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:24.870
Can I really...

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.480
The light is brighter than it was in the Duel Palace.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:39.460
Is it because Yuya and Hugo are 
closer than they were last night?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:43.980
Yuya...

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:49.180
Jack was certainly strong.

00:10:50.140 --> 00:10:53.370
Lightning Disobey of Rebellion!

00:10:59.690 --> 00:11:00.880
And the finish...

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:04.580
Go, Rune-Eyes Pendulum Dragon!

00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.280
Attack Jack Atlas directly!

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.130
I activated my Action Spell Evasive Evasion,

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:13.480
to Special Summon an Evasive Evasion Token.

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:17.710
Once per turn, an Evasive Evasion 
Token lets me negate one attack.

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:22.090
I used this to negate Rune-Eyes 
Pendulum Dragon's attack!

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:26.970
But Rune-Eyes attacks depending 
on the level of monsters

00:11:26.970 --> 00:11:28.970
used as components in its fusion.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:31.500
Trump Girl's Level 2 lets it attack twice.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:34.040
Therefore, it can attack once more!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.810
I attack Evasive Evasion Token!

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:40.040
I activate my trap, Reject Reborn!

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:44.490
I negate one of your monster's attacks, 
and end the Battle Phase!

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.140
He used Reject Reborn to end the Battle Phase.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.720
If he'd used that before Dark Rebellion's attack,

00:11:53.720 --> 00:11:56.870
he could have negated all of my attacks.

00:12:00.040 --> 00:12:01.000
But...

00:12:02.270 --> 00:12:08.310
Jack took Dark Rebellion's attack, 
leaving himself vulnerable to Rune-Eyes,

00:12:08.310 --> 00:12:11.010
so it'd look like he was about to lose.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:21.600
Then, I destroy all monsters 
on my side of the field,

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:25.770
to Special Summon, from the 
graveyard, as many monsters

00:12:25.770 --> 00:12:27.440
as I negated attacks from.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.390
What?

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:31.130
I negated two attacks!

00:12:31.670 --> 00:12:35.940
Be reborn, Red Wyvern! Red Resonator!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.780
Then he Synchro Summoned the two he resurrected.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:44.240
The cry of the champion shakes 
heaven and earth.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:47.770
Let the conqueror's unique power 
be carved into your body!

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:49.710
Synchro Summon!

00:12:50.480 --> 00:12:52.210
The raging soul...

00:12:52.210 --> 00:12:55.240
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:12:56.530 --> 00:13:00.110
Once per turn, Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:04.910
can destroy all Special Summoned monsters 
with lower attack points than its own.

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:09.590
And for each, it deals 500 
points of damage to you.

00:13:09.590 --> 00:13:11.770
Absolute Power Flame!

00:13:19.010 --> 00:13:22.030
Kneel before your king!

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:25.220
Red Hot Crimson Hell Burning!

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.160
On the very first turn, Jack set Reject Reborn.

00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.060
In other words,

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:42.890
I was in the palm of his hand from the very start.

00:13:46.980 --> 00:13:49.130
It all went as he'd planned it.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:51.540
Is that Jack's form of entertainment?

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.750
Nothing like me, who let Jack provoke me,

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:58.580
so that crushing him was all I could think of!

00:14:00.280 --> 00:14:01.920
Maybe Jack was right.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:05.270
Maybe I'm not on his level at all.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.480
Or on Dad's level, either.

00:14:08.420 --> 00:14:11.340
At this rate, I can't even make people here smile,

00:14:11.340 --> 00:14:13.830
let alone bring peace to the dimensions.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.360
Who's there?

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.010
Someone's there, right?

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.780
Answer me!

00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:37.320
It's me...

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.520
You?

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.900
The one who led you to the 
Duel Palace yesterday.

00:14:41.900 --> 00:14:43.000
Who led me?

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:50.750
Oh, were you told not to talk to me?

00:14:50.750 --> 00:14:53.720
No... Nothing like that.

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:56.340
What's your name?

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.260
Sam.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:01.550
Sam... Why did you give me this card?

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.560
I want you to give it back to Jack!

00:15:07.560 --> 00:15:12.040
After you win the Friendship Cup 
and fight him again!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:19.800
It's coming into sight.

00:15:20.260 --> 00:15:25.340
There are over 200,000 people 
filling the Duel Palace!

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:30.990
As they should, because the 
greatest duel festival in City,

00:15:30.990 --> 00:15:34.280
the Friendship Cup, is about to begin.

00:15:34.280 --> 00:15:38.030
Continuing to provide commentary 
after the opening ceremonies,

00:15:38.030 --> 00:15:41.710
I, Melissa Claire, now descend upon the venue!

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:43.020
One, two...

00:15:43.430 --> 00:15:47.850
City is united as one! We're all friends!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:16:00.140
You want me to return this card to Jack? Why?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:05.210
For us Commons, Jack was the star of hope.

00:16:06.840 --> 00:16:10.080
He grew up in the slums like we did,

00:16:10.080 --> 00:16:16.400
took part in the Friendship Cup, and took 
out Tops duelists, one after the next.

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.410
I admired him so much.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.990
Three years ago, he won,

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:26.340
becoming the first Commons-born King of Duelists.

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:29.370
I was as happy as if I were up there.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:35.870
But after that, Jack changed...

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:37.260
Changed?

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:43.850
Landing okay.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.520
Wow, I really am popular!

00:16:47.790 --> 00:16:51.040
Let's keep that energy up, as we 
introduce the sixteen duelists

00:16:51.040 --> 00:16:54.110
who will participate in this year's tournament.

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:55.530
First, this man!

00:16:56.560 --> 00:17:02.680
The novice entertainer, branded as 
a loser last night against the king.

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:06.290
Yuya Sakaki!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.030
Hey, I know he couldn't beat the king, 
but isn't that a bit cruel?

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:12.510
I don't write this stuff, okay?

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.490
Well, he really was a novice.

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:19.480
Next to Mr. Atlas, he's pretty sad.

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:30.170
After he was crowned as king, 
Jack became City's biggest star.

00:17:31.350 --> 00:17:34.740
City bestows incredible rewards upon "winners."

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:40.830
Since he kept winning, many companies 
and wealthy people approached him.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:45.500
Jack himself quickly amassed 
a great deal of wealth.

00:17:46.330 --> 00:17:50.230
At some point, he began to look 
down on us Commons.

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.040
Hey!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.380
Ow...

00:17:58.980 --> 00:18:00.740
You can't enter without permission!

00:18:02.090 --> 00:18:02.980
King!

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:09.720
Um, I've been a fan of yours for so long...

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:13.480
Ever since you were the best duelist in the slums.

00:18:14.200 --> 00:18:16.360
I want to be just like you.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.670
But right now, I have no cards or money...

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.940
That's why I'm rooting for you!

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.840
Please keep representing the Commons!

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.200
If you don't have one, I'll give you this.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:32.870
This card is the most suited to you.

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:37.080
That was this card?

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:41.500
A low-level monster, with weak attack points.

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:44.470
He said it was the monster most suited to me.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:48.320
He was looking down on me, even though 
we're both Commons.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:52.360
Jack's changed!

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:55.310
Jack Atlas became king and got rich.

00:18:55.310 --> 00:18:58.180
He's a traitor who sold his soul to the Tops!

00:18:58.660 --> 00:18:59.860
A traitor?

00:19:04.860 --> 00:19:09.950
Shinji Weber and Crow Hogan here 
were both born Commons.

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:13.830
Can they inherit Jack Atlas's legacy 
and become a star?

00:19:14.390 --> 00:19:19.070
What is she talking about? Atlas isn't 
a Commons anymore.

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:23.540
As long as he keeps winning, 
Jack is one of us Tops!

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:24.830
Jack, huh?

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:27.530
He's a traitor who sells himself to the Tops!

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:32.040
Hey, shut up! Jack is still a Commons hero!

00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:33.260
You want to step outside?

00:19:33.260 --> 00:19:34.290
What was that?

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:43.960
Jack became more and more full of himself,

00:19:43.960 --> 00:19:46.820
and eventually came to look 
down on everyone else.

00:19:47.860 --> 00:19:51.240
He has fans who think that's cool, but I...

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:56.230
That's why I was hoping you 
might beat him in my place.

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:58.440
Why me?

00:19:58.440 --> 00:20:01.180
You told him not to mock your duel.

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:03.860
I won't let you mock it, Jack!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:08.870
As someone who's suffered the 
humiliation of losing to him,

00:20:09.970 --> 00:20:13.420
I thought you might understand how I feel.

00:20:14.530 --> 00:20:15.670
Sam...

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:21.720
That concludes the introductions 
of the sixteen participants.

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.730
But you aren't listening at all...

00:20:24.730 --> 00:20:28.920
Hey, everyone! Don't you remember 
the tournament's slogan?

00:20:28.920 --> 00:20:32.980
"City is united as one! We're all friends!" Right?

00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:38.550
Fine! We don't have time, 
so I'll just move on, okay?

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:42.490
Anyway, it's time to begin the duels!

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:47.130
Out of the sixteen, the two who 
will open this first round are...

00:20:48.590 --> 00:20:52.300
Crow Hogan and Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:20:58.610 --> 00:21:03.130
I, the man Gongenzaka, will redeem Yuya's name.

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:10.570
I don't want to become a show for the Tops, but...

00:21:11.720 --> 00:21:13.530
Is Jack watching, too?

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:14.520
Yeah.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.330
I'll show that traitor

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:22.530
just how strong the bonds 
between Commons are.

00:21:24.480 --> 00:21:27.370
I'm working for the Tops now.

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:30.940
I know it isn't my place to speak.

00:21:31.750 --> 00:21:34.510
But I can't stand it!

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:38.250
I heard you came from another town, somewhere.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:43.800
I'm sorry for involving someone who 
isn't a Tops or Commons in this.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:49.300
But I thought you would understand how I feel.

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.460
I do...

00:21:51.460 --> 00:21:53.640
I really can't stand it, either.

00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:56.470
I want to be there for Sam.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:57.690
But...

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:00.040
Can I do it?

00:22:01.700 --> 00:22:03.060
As I am now...

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:08.550
Can I fight Jack again and win?

00:23:45.160 --> 00:23:49.000
Our first match's duelists are now arriving!

00:23:49.000 --> 00:23:52.110
They're Crow Hogan and Noboru Gongenzaka!

00:23:52.110 --> 00:23:56.210
The man Gongenzaka will show 
you the power of the Lancers.

00:23:56.210 --> 00:24:01.190
I'm going to win and show the 
kids what we can really do!

00:24:01.190 --> 00:24:04.460
The fight is about to start!

00:24:05.280 --> 00:24:11.030
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Opening Battle!! Crow Versus Gongenzaka.

00:24:11.030 --> 00:24:12.970
The fun is only getting started!
